			"Message": "build(Sky): Standardize VS Code workbench loading with /vs/ URL paths\n\nReplace @codeeditorland/output package specifiers with runtime /vs/ URL paths across all workbench entry points (Browser.astro, BrowserTest.astro, Mountain.astro, BrowserProxy/Workbench.ts).\n\nChanges:\n- Use /vs/code/browser/workbench/workbench.js (served from Sky/Public/vs → Output/Target/Microsoft/VSCode/vs symlink)\n- Apply is:inline to bypass Vite/Rollup bundling entirely for inline scripts\n- Use variable assignment (const WorkbenchUrl = \"/vs/...\") to make Rollup treat imports as truly dynamic (only string literals trigger analysis)\n- Add try/catch error handling with console.error for graceful failure\n- Update astro.config.ts external resolver to also match /vs/ prefix\n- Comment out Electron workbench import (not yet compiled in Output)\n\nThis resolves Rollup's inability to resolve package specifiers at build time while maintaining dynamic loading at runtime.",
			"SHA": "a4af28b0684223424ea0225224a8a4bd11da2434"
		}
